CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ outer handler reached after inner rethrow: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ inner rethrow re-propagates the inner exception E\(2\): SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[except.throw]/8 -- a bare `throw;` in the inner handler re-propagates the inner
exception E(2), the one that handler is handling, not the outer E(1).  Verifies
the per-handler current-exception slot is keyed to the innermost enclosing
handler (cross-checked against g++ and clang++).
